# Anything a lookup produced. Every one of these names real people, says what
# they paid for their home and, once logged in, when they were born - so the
# rule is deliberately blunt: no data file, anywhere in the tree, ever gets
# committed. Source lives in .py and .toml, so nothing here is a real cost.
out/
exports/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# The same output when --outdir, --out or --dump points somewhere else: CSVs,
# workbooks, whole property records as XML, older attester saved as text, raw
# dumps.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xml
*.txt
*.json
*-attester-*

# ...except the fixtures the tests are built on. Those are real documents with
# invented people in them, and they belong in the repository.
!tests/**

# Python
__pycache__/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
